{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1865"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge sport-games/football","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/sport-games__football.g1.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",68],["+","quickest way off the pitch is the red card, and even that has a history. Yellow and red cards, proposed by the English referee Ken Aston, were first used at the 1970 World Cup, where the only red card went not to a player but to the West "],["=",2],["+","physio Erich Deuser. It took until 1974 for a player to see red at a World Cup: Chile's Carlos Caszely was sent off against West Germany on 14 June 1974 for a retaliatory foul on Berti Vogts.\n\nThe German "],["=",1093]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",68],["+","Der schnellste Weg vom Platz ist die Rote Karte, und selbst sie hat eine Geschichte. Gelbe und Rote Karten, vorgeschlagen vom englischen Schiedsrichter Ken Aston, kamen erstmals bei der WM 1970 zum Einsatz, wo die einzige Rote Karte keinen Spieler traf, sondern den deutschen Physiotherapeuten Erich Deuser. Erst 1974 sah ein Spieler bei einer WM Rot: Chiles Carlos Caszely wurde am 14. Juni 1974 gegen die Bundesrepublik nach einem Revanchefoul an Berti Vogts vom Platz gestellt.\n\n"],["=",1027]]}]},
{"seq":3,"at":"2026-10-21","kind":"corrected","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1865"},"reason":"a1865: bodyEn/De (Effenberg): \"the Gladbach midfielder\" → \"the Fiorentina player\" (he played for Fiorentina in 1994, returned to Gladbach after the World Cup); \"substituted in the second half\" → \"in the 75th minute\"; \"a gesture that was caught by the television cameras\" → \"that the television cameras missed but the stands did not\" (the scene happened outside the TV pictures); \"until Erich Ribbeck recalled him in 1998\" → \"until a brief comeback under Vogts in September 1998\" (last cap v Romania, 5 Sep 1998, under Vogts) — https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Effenberg","by":"enrich batch 200","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-enrich/enrich-report/a1048-a2580.md","sources":[{"url":"https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Effenberg"}]},
